   "title": "Typical operating circuit and capacitor values",
   "page": 10,
   "description": "The full hookup on a 5 V rail. C1 sits across C1+/C1- and C2 across C2+/C2- as the charge pump's flying capacitors; C3 is the reservoir on V+ and C4 the reservoir on V-, each returned to ground; CBYPASS decouples VCC at pins 16 and 15. DIN1 and DIN2 come from the UART and leave inverted on DOUT1 and DOUT2 at RS-232 levels; RIN1 and RIN2 come in from the cable and return inverted on ROUT1 and ROUT2. Each receiver input has its 5 kΩ load to ground inside the chip.",
